      },
      "worked": "The top row gives the common sum: $2+(-5)+0=-3$.\n\nThe known corners of the descending diagonal sum to $2+(-4)=-2$, so the centre is $-1$.\n\nIn the ascending diagonal, $0+(-1)=-1$, so the bottom-left entry is $-2$.\n\nIn the right column, $0+(-4)=-4$, so the middle-right entry is $1$.\n\nIn the bottom row, $-2+(-4)=-6$, so the bottom-middle entry is $3$.\n\nIn the left column, $2+(-2)=0$, so the middle-left entry is $-3$.\n\nCheck the remaining lines: $-3+(-1)+1=-3$ and $-5+(-1)+3=-3$. Thus all three rows, all three columns and both diagonals sum to $-3$.",
